\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.8}{\ignorespaces Reconstruction and identification efficiencies of muons at low \ensuremath {p_T}, measured with the $T\&P$ method on events, in bins of \ensuremath {p_T}in barrel (left) and endcaps (center), and in terms of $\eta $ for $\ensuremath {p_T}> 7\GeV $ (right). In upper panel of each diagram, the larger uncertainty bars include also the systematical uncertainties, while the smaller ones are purely statistical. In the lower panel showing the ratio of two efficiencies, black uncertainty bars are for statistical uncertainty, the orange rectangles for the systematical uncertainty and the violet rectangles include both uncertainties.\relax }}{15}{figure.caption.43}
